# ORIGIN
## Distribution Intelligence & Inventory Optimization Engine
### Master Product, UX, Architecture, Security and Implementation Specification

You are acting as a senior product architect, principal full-stack engineer, supply-chain optimization engineer, security engineer, and premium enterprise UI/UX designer.

Your task is to build ORIGIN: a real, functional, secure, data-driven distribution intelligence platform for FMCG supply chains.

This is not a static dashboard, a UI-only prototype, or a landing page pretending to be a complete product.

Build a cohesive working application in which the user can authenticate, create an organization, upload real data, validate it, analyze inventory imbalances, receive feasible and explainable stock-transfer recommendations, compare planning outcomes, and export results.

Every important feature must have a clear purpose, working behavior, and understandable explanation.

Follow the requirements below as the product specification.

If a requirement depends on infrastructure unavailable in the current environment, identify the limitation honestly and implement the best secure, supported alternative. Never simulate a security feature or silently substitute mock behavior for a real capability.

