# 2. DESIGN DIRECTION: PREMIUM, CLEAN, CLASSIC

The interface must look like a carefully designed premium software product.

Use the clarity, restraint, typography, spacing, and interaction quality associated with excellent Google products and the ChatGPT web interface as general design inspiration.

Do not directly copy either product's interface.

Create an original visual identity for ORIGIN.

## 2.1 White theme

Use a white-first visual system.

Preferred foundation:
- White main canvas.
- Soft off-white secondary surfaces where useful.
- Dark charcoal or near-black primary text.
- Restrained neutral borders.
- Muted gray supporting text.
- One consistent, sophisticated accent color.
- Semantic colors for risk, success, warnings, and errors.

Avoid:
- Dark mode as the default.
- Excessive gradients.
- Rainbow colors.
- Excessive saturated backgrounds.
- Large decorative color blocks.
- Unnecessary glassmorphism.
- Heavy shadows around every component.
- Generic AI-generated dashboard aesthetics.

The application must feel calm, precise, modern, and trustworthy.

## 2.2 Floating navigation and tabs

Create a refined navigation system with floating or softly elevated navigation elements where appropriate.

Navigation may use:
- A clean sidebar on desktop.
- Compact, clearly selected navigation states.
- Subtle floating action bars where they improve usability.
- Mobile-friendly navigation on smaller screens.
- Carefully placed contextual action panels.

Do not make every element float.

Do not use excessive pill-shaped controls or oversized rounded cards.

Use floating surfaces only when they improve hierarchy, focus, or interaction.

Selected tabs may have a subtle translucent or softly blurred background.

Use blur sparingly, primarily for:
- Selected navigation states.
- Small contextual overlays.
- Occasional floating panels.
- Focused onboarding overlays.

Keep text and important data fully legible.

## 2.3 Typography

Typography is a major part of the product identity.

Use a clean, premium sans-serif font system. Prefer a reliable modern typeface such as Inter or an equivalent available font.

Establish a consistent hierarchy:

- Large editorial-style headings for page introductions.
- Bold, confident headings for major sections.
- Clear medium-sized headings for panels.
- Highly readable body text.
- Compact but legible labels.
- Tabular numerals for inventory quantities, costs, percentages, and comparisons.

Use large typography selectively.

For example, an Overview page may introduce itself with:

"See your distribution network clearly."

A Risk Analysis page may use:

"Find the next stockout before it happens."

These are examples of design tone, not mandatory marketing claims.

Large centered typography may be used on:
- The public landing page.
- Authentication screens.
- Empty states.
- First-run onboarding.
- Important workflow introductions.

Do not center every heading or make ordinary operational tables oversized.

