# 17. SECURITY AND PRIVACY

Implement security as part of the architecture, not as a final cosmetic step.

Requirements include:
- Real authentication.
- Backend authorization.
- Organization isolation.
- Secure storage access.
- Input validation.
- Safe file processing.
- Protected secrets.
- Appropriate access rules.
- Safe error handling.
- Protection against unauthorized record access.
- Data deletion or retention behavior consistent with implemented functionality.

Never trust an organization ID, role, user ID, or permission supplied by the client without validating it against the authenticated server-side identity.

Never allow a user to elevate their own privileges by changing a frontend value.

Use the security controls appropriate to the selected backend and authentication provider.

Do not claim that the application is production-secure without testing its security boundaries.

